From 4a74c1ea05a2517f3e512fb142048bd188c1e917 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:02:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/69] LOCAL: arm64: configs: nairo: Build in gpucc, disable
 DMABUF_DEBUG

The GPU SMMU gives up on the GPU clock controller after the 10 s
deferred probe timeout and is never retried, so build the clock
controller in.

CONFIG_DMABUF_DEBUG (default y with DEBUG_KERNEL) hands importers a copy
of the sg table with the CPU side cleared, while msm maps imported
buffers from sg_phys() and sg->length: every buffer shared with
simpledrm was mapped as nothing and the GPU faulted on it.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config b/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config
index b1d0b9414..d1bced882 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config
@@ -41,3 +41,7 @@ CONFIG_QCOM_SPMI_TEMP_ALARM=y
 CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_NT36XXX_SPI=m
 # PM7250B SMB5 charger (qcom_smbx + SMB5 v4 series), module loaded by hand
 CONFIG_CHARGER_QCOM_SMB2=m
+# Adreno 620: the GPU SMMU needs its clock controller before the deferred probe timeout
+CONFIG_SM_GPUCC_8250=y
+# Strips the CPU side of imported sg tables; msm maps imports from it
+# CONFIG_DMABUF_DEBUG is not set
